(417, '120363403706171703@g.us', 'UNITÉ DES ETUDIANTS DE MPANDA ', '*IYI GROUPE IHURIKIYEMWO ABANYESHURE BO MURI KOMINE NZIZA YA MPANDA BIGA MUMAKAMINUZA ATANDUKANYE*\n\n*AMATEGEKO AGENGA GROUPE*\n\n*1.BIRABUJIJWE KURUNGIKA STICKERS MURI GROUPE*\n*2.BIRABUJIJWE KUVUGA AUDIO MURI GROUPE*\n*3.BIRABUJIJWE KURUNGIKA VIDÉOS CANKE PHOTO Z\'IBITERASONI MURI GROUPE*\n*4.BIRABUJIJWE KURUNGIKA PHOTO ITAGIRA INSIGURO MURI GROUPE*\n*5.BIRABUJIJWE GUTERANA AMAJAMBO MURI GROUPE*\n*6. BIRABUJIJWE KUZANA VYA POLITIQUE MURI IYI GROUPE*\n\n*AYO MATEGEKO ASHIZWEHO  KUGIRANGO UBUMWE BUBANDANYE BUSASAGARA MUBANYESHURE BO MURI KOMINE NZIZA YA MPANDA  BIGA MUMAKAMINUZA ATANDUKANYE*', 1, '2026-03-29 23:59:49', '2026-03-29 23:59:49'),
(418, '120363173806656380@g.us', '2nd group of American Center Bujumbura ', 'OPEN FROM MONDAY TO THURSDAY at 9AM till 4PM.\n\nThe American Center Bujumbura is the research and information service of the Public Affairs Section of the U.S. Embassy, The Center provides up-to-date information about the United States, including its policies, its social and political processes, and its people.  \n\nIts main aim is to reflect contemporary America to Burundi and the Center’s resources are intended to meet the information needs of university students, government and community leaders, journalists, researchers, academics and other professionals interested in the United States.  Most of our programs are offered in English.\n\nMembership is free and open to the public. Members must be residents in Burundi. Register online for membership at the link below on the screen! Membership is 100% free, and after registering you will be able to attend programs, use the computers and the internet, and borrow books.\n\nYou can apply for the membership by completing the online Membership form.\n\nAVAILABLE RESOURCES\n\nThe American Center offers the following resources:\n\n- a reference collection in French and English of books on economics, history and culture, politics and international relations, literature, science and technology\n\n- a range of current magazines and periodicals\n\n- Internet access on five computer work stations\n\n- American films and documentaries. Visitors may watch videos using the in-house viewing facilities. Group screenings can be arranged upon request.\n\n- Programs on contemporary topics and special events that provide the American perspective.\n\nhttps://bi.usembassy.gov/education-culture/american-spaces/irc/', 1, '2026-03-29 23:59:49', '2026-03-30 03:00:45'),
